---
import Header from "../../components/Header.astro";
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import { DOCS_NAV, REPO } from "../../scripts/catalog.mjs";
---

<Base title="Link the words to the steps · motion-kit docs" description="Pattern: terms in your text point at steps of the diagram, by hover, focus and tap, with keyboard access.">
<Header page="docs" />
<main class="docs" id="main">
	<nav class="docs-nav" aria-label="Docs">
		{DOCS_NAV.map((g) => (
			<div><h2>{g.title}</h2><ul>{g.items.map((i) => <li><a href={i.href} aria-current={i.current ? "page" : undefined}>{i.label}</a></li>)}</ul></div>
		))}
	</nav>
	<article class="article">
		<p class="crumbs">Patterns / Hover and focus linking</p>
		<h1>Link the words to the steps</h1>
		<p class="lede">Terms in your text point at parts of the diagram. Hovering, focusing or tapping a term jumps the diagram to that step; the active step marks the term back. It works by keyboard and on touch, because every term is a button.</p>

		<section aria-labelledby="try-h"><h2 id="try-h">Try it</h2>
			<div class="demo">
				<p id="demo-text"></p>
				<div class="player-box" id="demo-stage"></div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section aria-labelledby="build-h"><h2 id="build-h">Build it</h2>
			<p class="lede small">Mount the player as usual, keep its controller, mark terms with <code>data-mk-step</code> (a step id or index) and bind them with <code>linkSteps</code>. Use buttons, not spans, so the terms are reachable without a mouse.</p>
			<div class="codecard"><div class="file">page.html</div><pre tabindex="0"><code set:html={`&lt;p&gt;The &lt;button type="button" data-mk-step="0"&gt;home hub&lt;/button&gt; switches the
   &lt;button type="button" data-mk-step="1"&gt;lights&lt;/button&gt; …&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div id="home"&gt;&lt;!-- server-rendered final frame --&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;script type="module"&gt;
  import { mountPlayer } from "./motion-kit/runtime/player.mjs";
  import { linkSteps } from "./motion-kit/runtime/links.mjs";
  const player = mountPlayer(home, scene, { autoplay: "none" });
  const dispose = linkSteps(player, document.querySelector("article"));
&lt;/script&gt;`} /></pre></div>
			<ul>
				<li>Hover (mouse and pen), keyboard focus and click select the same step. Touch selects on tap; never hover-only.</li>
				<li>A selection jumps to a settled frame, so the diagram never shows a half-drawn state. <code>{`{ animate: true }`}</code> plays forward instead, except under reduced motion.</li>
				<li>The step stays when the pointer leaves; <code>{`{ restore: true }`}</code> makes hover and focus a preview that returns to the previous frame, and a click keeps its step.</li>
				<li><code>linkSteps</code> marks the terms of the step it selected with <code>aria-current="step"</code>. This page also follows the player’s own buttons, so it polls <code>controller.time</code> against the scene’s steps and passes <code>{`{ mark: false }`}</code>: <b>needs: player step-change event</b>.</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<section id="explore" aria-labelledby="exp-h"><h2 id="exp-h">Then: make it explorable</h2>
			<p class="lede small">A control can change the spec itself. The parameter is input, not state: the page re-creates the scene and seeks the same step, so every frame is still a pure function of t.</p>
			<div class="demo">
				<label class="slider"><b>Integrations</b><input id="spokes" type="range" min="2" max="7" step="1" value="4"><span class="mono" id="spokes-text"></span></label>
				<div class="player-box" id="explore-stage"></div>
				<div class="codecard"><pre tabindex="0"><code set:html={`slider.oninput = () =&gt; {
  const step = stepIndexAt(scene, player.time);   // keep the reader’s place
  const spec = { ...base, spokes: base.spokes.slice(0, slider.value) };
  scene = createScene(spec, { format });
  player = mountPlayer(el, scene, { autoplay: "none" });
  if (step < 0) player.seek(0);                   // before the first step
  else player.seekStep(Math.min(step, scene.steps.length - 1));
};`} /></pre></div>
				<p class="needs-note">Reading the current step needs a getter: <b>needs: controller.step getter</b>.</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<nav class="pager" aria-label="Pager"><a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/skills/animated-diagram/references/interactivity.md`}>← Step buttons and caption</a><a href="/#scroll">Scroll-driven steps →</a></nav>
	</article>
</main>
</Base>
<script>import "../../scripts/docs.mjs";</script>
